 "variant": "RX in the corner (ua[3] / ua[2]), TX on ua[4] / ua[5]",
 "note": "Matt's tall-chain layout reworked (2026-11-14): rx_t as laid out (chain + one-row log_det_t, unflipped: input at the west end, flowing east), RX on ua[3] / ua[2] so the input section sits bottom-left, TX drivers on ua[4] / ua[5] in the strip west of it (TX is off in RX, so no isolation needed), dbg on ua[1]. det comes out at the detector's west end: LPF, averager, comparator, Ctrim and the trim DAC run east along the top towards the macro. Everything but the macro shifted 15 um west (bias 21 um from the macro halo; the RX inputs run ~15 um west along the bottom from ua[2] / ua[1] to the chain). Detector at exactly rx_t's offset (-7.7, +70.4 from the chain); bias R90 at (206.7, 3) just clear of it, 17.8 um of decap between the bias and the macro. Bias east of the chain's output end (ib_chain / vcm run west along the bottom to the chain's south-edge pins). Pinout change: rx ua[0]/ua[1] -> ua[3]/ua[2], tx ua[3]/ua[4] -> ua[4]/ua[5], dbg ua[2] -> ua[1] (under the chain). Rule 2's 4 um is the flyline of o4 past stage 1; the real taps are wired in rx_t's channel (PEX: nothing back to the input).",
